---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../../data/site.json';
---
<Base title="FieldADE privacy policy" description="What the FieldADE iPhone app and HomeADE collect, where your data goes, and what Embry Development never sees.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>FieldADE privacy policy</h1>
      <p><em>Last updated November 13, 2026</em></p>

      <p>FieldADE is an iPhone app, with an optional Mac app called HomeADE, made by {site.legalName}. This page covers both.</p>
      <p><strong>The short version:</strong> Embry Development collects nothing. There is no account, no analytics, no advertising, and no tracking. Your notes, chats, and keys stay on your own devices, and when the app talks to an AI service it talks to that service directly with your own key.</p>
      <p>The App Store privacy label lists user content (messages, emails and texts, photos, and audio) as "linked to you" because Anthropic and xAI receive what you send them under your own account and may keep it for a time under their own policies. None of it reaches Embry Development, and none of it is used for tracking.</p>

      <h2>What stays on your devices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Your vault.</strong> The app reads and edits the notes folder you pick, on your phone or in iCloud Drive. Those files never come to us.</li>
        <li><strong>Your API keys.</strong> An Anthropic key you enter is kept in the iPhone Keychain. It goes only to Anthropic, with each request you make.</li>
        <li><strong>Chats.</strong> Chat history is saved in the app's own storage on your phone, or on your Mac if you run a chat there.</li>
        <li><strong>Calendar.</strong> The app shows your Google and iCloud calendars. If you sign in to Google in the app, it reads your calendars and events through Google's Calendar API with read-only access. If you sign in to iCloud, it reads them from Apple's iCloud calendar server with an app-specific password you make. Without a sign-in, and if you allow it, it reads the calendars already on the device. Events, sign-in tokens, and passwords stay on your devices, in the Keychain and your iCloud Keychain, and never come to us.</li>
        <li><strong>Speech.</strong> When you tap the mic, Apple's speech recognition turns your words into text, on the phone when the phone supports it.</li>
        <li><strong>Camera.</strong> Used only to scan a pairing code or to take a photo you choose to send in a chat.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Where data goes when you use a feature</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Anthropic.</strong> When you chat, your message, any photo you attach, and the notes the assistant reads to answer it are sent to Anthropic's API under your key. When you ask for an AI reply to an email or text, your HomeADE sends that message to Anthropic the same way. Anthropic's handling is set out in its own privacy policy at anthropic.com.</li>
        <li><strong>Google and Apple calendars.</strong> When you sign in to a calendar account, the app reads it straight from Google or Apple under that account. It only reads; it never changes or shares your events. FieldADE's use of information received from Google APIs adheres to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements.</li>
        <li><strong>xAI.</strong> A voice call, if you set one up, streams your voice from the phone through your own Mac to xAI's API under your key.</li>
        <li><strong>Your HomeADE.</strong> If you pair the phone with HomeADE, the phone talks to that Mac, which you own and run.</li>
        <li><strong>Apple.</strong> For widget updates and notifications, the phone gives its push token to your own HomeADE, which sends pushes through Apple's push service.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The relay</h2>
      <p>To reach your Mac away from home, the app can route traffic through relay.embry.dev, a service we run on Cloudflare. Traffic is encrypted end to end with a key that only your phone and your Mac hold, so the relay cannot read it. The relay stores two things per HomeADE: a hash of its key and the time it last connected. Cloudflare, as the host, may keep standard connection logs such as IP addresses for a short time.</p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>FieldADE is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly collect data from anyone.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If this policy changes, the new version will appear on this page with a new date.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
